Character artwork and recordings
--------------------------------

The upstream project's `ASSET_RIGHTS.md` states that no separate permission to
copy, modify or redistribute the character images, designs or audio has been
granted, and that the characters derive from third-party works whose rights
holders have not licensed this use.

In deference to that:

  * **This repository contains no asset bytes.** The artwork lives in the
    upstream submodule, and `.gitignore` excludes the generated
    `Sources/NuonuoChuubyCore/Asset/AssetManifest.swift`.
  * That manifest is generated from the submodule at build time and compiled
    into the binary. It carries only the *paths* of the files and the pinned
    commit, and is never committed.
  * A development build (`make run` / `rerun`) hard-links the artwork out of the
    submodule, so nothing is copied.
  * A release build downloads the artwork on first launch, from a jsdelivr CDN
    pinned to the commit recorded in the manifest.

Redistribution of the artwork is therefore not performed by this project; the
underlying rights status is unchanged and remains unresolved. Anyone shipping a
build carries that same status.


Third-party code
----------------

No third-party Swift packages are used. The package has no external
dependencies; everything is built on Apple's frameworks (AppKit, CoreGraphics,
CoreServices, AVFoundation) plus the Swift standard library.

